{
  // `noUnusedLocals` (D165) — THE WORKER HALF OF THE GAP D164 CLOSED ON THE SPA,
  // and it was demonstrated rather than predicted.
  //
  // D164 armed `noUnusedLocals` in `frontend/tsconfig.json` and `no-unused-vars`
  // in `eslint.config.mjs`. Both are scoped to the SPA — the ESLint glob is
  // `frontend/src/**/*.{js,jsx}` and that tsconfig includes `frontend/src` only —
  // so after eighteen unused-declaration alerts were swept, `cloudflare-worker/src`
  // still had **no unused-local check of any kind**. `check-unused-imports.mjs`
  // reaches this tree but sees only imports and `const {` destructures, never a
  // plain `const x = …`.
  //
  // D165 produced the first instance that gap let through, in its own diff:
  // consolidating a `jwt_min_iat` write into `bumpJwtMinIat` left the floor it
  // used to bind assigned to a local nothing read. Every local check passed;
  // CodeQL caught it on the PR, which is the slow way round.
  //
  // TWO findings across the whole worker, and the second one is the argument for
  // the flag rather than a cost of it. The first was D165's own binding above.
  // The second was pre-existing: `routes/positions.ts` imported the type `User`
  // and used it nowhere.
  //
  // THAT ONE NAMES A THIRD BLIND SPOT, beside the two D164 measured.
  // `check-unused-imports.mjs` DOES reach this tree, and still could not see it:
  // its detection is `^import\s+(?:[\w$]+\s*,\s*)?\{`, which needs the brace
  // straight after the keyword (or a default import and a comma first), so in
  // `import type { Env, User }` the word `type` sits exactly where the brace has
  // to be. **`import type { … }` is invisible to that regex by construction.**
  // Widening the regex is the wrong fix and is deliberately not done: `import
  // type` is TypeScript-only, so this flag — on both tsconfigs — already covers
  // every file that can contain one, and it decides by scope analysis rather
  // than by pattern. That is the argument `eslint.config.mjs` makes at length
  // for preferring a real checker to a third bespoke script.
  //
  // With both cleared, `tsc` reports zero. One line, on a check `test:drift`
  // already runs as `test:types`.
  //
  // (The first measurement of this said "exactly one", because it grepped the
  // CLI run for TS6133 — an unused LOCAL — and an unused type is TS6196. The
  // flag in the config reports both; a grep scoped to one code was the reason
  // the count looked smaller than it was.)
  //
  // `noUnusedParameters` stays OFF, as on the SPA and for its reason: it flags
  // positional handler parameters that cannot be dropped without changing what
  // the rest bind to.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ES2022",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": ["@cloudflare/workers-types"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "jsxImportSource": "hono/jsx",
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
